{
  "abstract": "Over half of known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. Parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$ makes the regular fifths linear in the trace $S_{ab}$, and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$, cutting out the Branch-1 sextuple surface $E_{Br1}$ and twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and the first rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$ of relation type $(5,2)$. Factoring the four-variable regular relation defines $S_{4,2}$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. Beyond fixed-quintuple fibres, we establish Master Syzygies unifying DKMS, Chebyshev, paired/antipodal sources, the universal $(C_0,w_1)$ osculating surface $S_7^{univ}(q,\\Lambda)$ ($18/21$-compatible over $w_1(q) = (q^2-3)/(2q)$, whose sign group $V_4$ spans four $19/21$-compatible branches of $\\Delta_-\\Delta_+ = 0$ and four twin-fifth branches), and the osculating tower $S_7^{osc,(n)}(R,\\kappa)$. On the master biquadratic curve, Vieta jumping is a QRT elliptic translation $Q_{n-1} = [n]P_\\infty \\oplus T_0$ on the monic Weierstrass cubic $E_W(R^2,Z)$, with even multiplier $\\mu_n(R^2,Z)$, $2$-descent square telescoping, and disjointness of $\\Delta_- = 0$ and $\\Delta_+ = 0$ away from $R \\in \\{0,\\pm 1\\}, B_W = 0$. At $Z = 8(R+1)$, formal-group logarithm non-vanishing proves $n=1$ is the unique degenerate level. For all $n \\ge 2$, canonical septuples $S_7^{can,(n)}(r)$ ($\\ge 18/21$ squares) and pools $U_{14}^{can,(n)}(r)$ ($\\ge 34/91$ in $\\mathbb{Q}(r)$, $\\ge 35/91$ on $5r^2-1=\\rho^2$; exact at $n=2,3$) are non-degenerate and distinct, with mirror duals $\\widehat{S}_7^{mir,(n)}(w) = -S_7^{can,(n)}(-R)|_{R=1-2w^2}$ ($\\ge 18/21$ and $\\ge 34/91$ in $\\mathbb{Q}(w)$, $\\ge 35/91$ on $5w^2-1=\\rho^2$), denominator degrees $\\binom{n+1}{2}$ for $1 \\le n \\le 8$, and smooth hyperelliptic gate curves of genus $g \\ge 5$ for $n \\in \\{2,3,4,5\\}$, finite by Faltings' theorem. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "This revision rigorously addresses all points in review_v30_final_result.json: (1) Restored the full specialization hypotheses in Section 9(b) for the Chebyshev compatibility counts, specifying that the increase from >= 12N + 2 to >= 12N + 3 automatic squares requires either the osculating section t = t_{b,v_0(m)}(r) or the intersection C_2 cap L_2: {Q(v_0) = 4*r^2, eta(v_0) = 1/(2*r)} over 5*r^2 - 1 = rho^2, and that >= 12N + 4 requires both conditions simultaneously over Q(q), while writing 17/21-compatible septuples rather than almost septuples; (2) Corrected the printed Level-2 mirror anchor formula in Supplement Theorem 20(113) to hat{b}_2^{mir}(w) = -(R^2 - 1)*(2*R^2 - 1)/(R*(2*R - 1)) for R = 1 - 2*w^2 (giving -1552/35 at w = 2, matching exp84); (3) Corrected the canonical Weierstrass curve parameters AW_can, BW_can, XW_Pinf, YW_Pinf in exp87 Part 3 to match exp84, verifying YW_Pinf^2 == XW_Pinf*(XW_Pinf^2 + AW_can*XW_Pinf + BW_can) and carrying the open-set exclusions R notin {0, +-1}, B_W != 0 into Section 9(c); and (4) Restricted Item 45's heading and the exp86 docstring to n in {2, 3, 4, 5}, added exact square-denominator assertions for all 12 residual gate conditions in exp86, stated all-level compatibility counts as guaranteed lower bounds (>= 18/21, >= 34/91 in Q(r) or Q(w), and >= 35/91 on 5*r^2 - 1 = rho^2 or 5*w^2 - 1 = rho^2, with exactness certified at n = 2, 3), and preserved compatibility qualifiers throughout.",
